@startsalt
' Screen: API Token Management
' User Stories:
'   - As a developer, I want to create API tokens scoped to specific roles
'   - As a developer, I want to see token metadata: creation, expiry, last used
'   - As a developer, I want to copy a new token exactly once after creation
'   - As a developer, I want to revoke or rotate existing tokens

{
  ' Top nav
  {
    <b>codefre.sh</b> | Scripts | Runs | Review Queue | <b>Settings</b>
    .
    <i>Acme Engineering</i> | keith@noizu.com
  }
  ==
  {
    <b>Organization Settings — Acme Engineering</b>
  }
  --
  {
    ' Sidebar
    {+
      <b>Settings</b>
      --
      General
      Members
      <b>API Tokens</b>
      SSO
      Freeball
      Webhooks
      Audit Log
    }
    |
    ' Content
    {
      <b>API Tokens</b>
      ==
      ' One-time display area (shown immediately after token creation)
      {+
        <color:green><b>Token Created — Copy Now</b></color>
        <i>This token will not be shown again. Store it securely.</i>
        --
        "cfsh_live_k9x2mTqA8vBnRdLpWcZeYoJhGfUs3iN1   " [Copy]
        --
        <i>Token: ci-pipeline-prod | Role: Editor | Expires: 2027-05-12</i>
      }
      ==
      ' Create form
      {+
        <b>Create New Token</b>
        --
        {
          Name: "ci-pipeline-prod                   " | Role: ^Editor^ | Expires: ^In 1 year^
        }
        [+ Create Token]
        <i>Token will have the permissions of the selected role. Name must be unique within the org.</i>
      }
      ==
      ' Token table
      {#
        <b>Name</b> | <b>Role</b> | <b>Created</b> | <b>Expires</b> | <b>Last Used</b> | <b>Actions</b>
        ci-pipeline-prod | Editor | 2026-05-12 | 2027-05-12 | <color:green>2026-05-12 09:14</color> | [Revoke] [Rotate]
        staging-runner | Viewer | 2026-03-01 | 2027-03-01 | 2026-05-10 18:33 | [Revoke] [Rotate]
        legacy-webhook | Admin | 2025-11-20 | <color:red>2026-05-01 (expired)</color> | 2026-04-30 | [Revoke]
      }
      --
      <i>3 tokens. Expired tokens cannot make API calls but are shown for audit purposes.</i>
      ==
      ' Rotate confirmation inline
      {+
        <b>Rotate Token — ci-pipeline-prod</b>
        --
        <i>Rotating generates a new secret. The old secret is immediately invalidated.\nUpdate your CI/CD configuration before rotating.</i>
        --
        [Confirm Rotation] | [Cancel]
      }
    }
  }
}

@endsalt
